The Composery automation API, server to menu.

- Server endpoints: /_composery/api/v1/... (API-key auth, in-process on the
  single port). Mounted before the VS Code catch-all so it is not swallowed;
  gated by the persistence-readiness middleware.
- Pty host exposure: the VS Code server hands its IPtyService to the embedder,
  so API-created terminals are ordinary persistent VS Code terminals instead
  of a parallel implementation. The API can explicitly ask its inventory for
  every persistent terminal without changing the editor's orphan-only restore
  query. API-created terminals carry
  API_TERMINAL_WORKSPACE_ID - belonging to no window, they belong to whichever
  window asks: layout merge adopts them (except while detaching, so Detach
  Session is not silently undone) and inventory events reach every client, not
  just the owning workspace's. Keep the id in sync with
  routes/api/terminals.ts; a test pins the two together.
- An API attachment is an ordinary terminal client, so it shares the per-client
  viewport and flow control the pty host already arbitrates (terminal-clients.diff)
  rather than bringing its own.
- Home-menu entry for managing API keys; the command itself lives in the
  composery-api builtin extension.

